=== B1 forensics: why every production deploy fails at 'Apply migrations on the server' ===

The chain, each link evidenced below:
 1. M13 contract task 1 rule: no shipped migration may be edited; numbers never reused.
    'Confirm one complete migration series ... no shipped migration edited.'
 2. PR1's merge (7847cc9, PR #57, 2026-09-20 09:33 UTC) EDITED migrations/003_reference_seed.sql
    (+6/-1: 003 now seeds Monday for business directly). 051 was correctly added as the
    carrier for already-seeded databases, but 003 was rewritten underneath it.
 3. The live schema_migrations row for 003 holds the OLD file's sha256. The Migrator compares
    hashes and refuses drift without an explicit force; the deploy step never forces:
      'Refusing to skip : checksum changed. Create a new migration or force.'
    public/migrate.php only forces when ?force is present in the request; deploy.yml calls it
    without the parameter (curl -fsS -H X-Migrate-Token .../public/migrate.php).
 4. So the apply loop throws before touching 051-054. The grep for 'MIGRATE OK' fails,
    the step exits 1, and every deploy since has failed identically.

