=== Consequences on the live host, in plain terms:
  Files uploaded, migrations not applied, 7 deploys since 09:33 UTC: live CODE contains
  PR1/PR2/PR4/PR6/PR8 changes; live SCHEMA stops at 050. Products.source_region,
  order_items.snapshot_category_id, contact_messages.is_staff_initiated and the 052 template
  update have never run there. M13 Section 11.2 trigger 'a failed or partially applied
  migration' is ACTIVE on production right now. Until B1 is resolved there is no path to a
  gated deploy, and PR7's live items (verify.sh re-proof, cron timestamp check, controlled
  Paystack transaction) cannot be scheduled honestly.

=== Remedies, in order of preference (decision belongs to the technical release owner;
=== PR7 recommends, it does not act on live):
  R1 (recommended): a corrective PR that restores migrations/003_reference_seed.sql to its
     shipped (pre-#57) bytes and lets 051 carry Monday for every database, fresh or existing.
     051 already does exactly that (INSERT business Monday ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE is_active),
     and fresh databases run the full chain 000..054 anyway, so 051 lands the decision in both
     worlds. The only loss is that a ZERO-from-scratch database no longer gets Monday inside the
     003 seed itself; it gets it one migration later, at 051, which the fresh-migration proof
     (gate section 1) covers in full. This keeps 'no shipped migration is ever edited' intact
     and unsticks every deploy without touching the live database by hand.
  R2 (rejected here): operator runs migrate.php?force once. Force RE-APPLIES the modified
     003 to the LIVE database and permanently records the new checksum. 003 is seed-only
     INSERT ... ON DUPLICATE-key style, but a re-run of an edited shipped file against live
     is exactly the improvised action contract Section 11.3 forbids: 'never improvised ... SQL
     and never an unproved down-migration'.
  R3: accept the drift by re-baselining - requires Owner sign-off, new migration numbering
     from 055, and the M13 Section 17 task-1 rule recorded as consciously amended. Heaviest.
